  "decision": "Keep existing geometry default and original model. Mixed-only fine-tuned checkpoint improves held-out instance recall but regresses close-up single-box masks, so remains an experimental candidate. Multi-size geometric fitting and downstream association still need work.",
  "limitations": [
    "Six development/test random nine-carton scenes are a small engineering sample, not a general success guarantee.",
    "Minimum 80 visible pixels and mask IoU>=0.5, one-to-one matching. Entirely hidden boxes are not counted as visible misses.",
    "Both full-view and equal depth-defined workspace ROI scores retained; model only receives RGB.",
    "No independent per-pixel labels for old single-box motion data; geometry masks are not used as truth.",
    "The held-out evaluation uses all nine raw camera frames, including one omitted from polygon training-format export.",
    "Current 3-D estimator retains the fixed reference-size prior. Improved segmentation is not multi-size grasping capability."
